kb:rx-what-to-check
    rdf:type <urn:kbase:type/Concept> ;
    rdfs:label "What to check" ;
    rdfs:comment "Demonstrates F269.1 (every local job detailed in This device). THIS IS A FIXTURE, not this machine: invented jobs and made-up run records, generated by scripts/agent/queue-to-space.ts --device from fixture worker and done files. 1) Find the job nodes: each carries its state (running, queued, held with a reason, given-up). \"room-scan\" should be running, \"describe-entities\" queued and waiting on it, \"weekly-summary\" held, \"flaky-export\" given-up. 2) Open \"link-check\": it ran 26 times, so it should show its 20 newest runs as nodes and a count for the older six. 3) Open a failed run: it should show how it ended. The \"room-scan\" run that made a splat names its output id. 4) Weakness to know: the real This device space does not exist yet (F269), and nothing schedules this script, so the real device file is not here." ;
    pred:demonstrates "F269.1" .

